ramify 1
// The application root: the Node entry, the configured protocol runtimes, and
// the assembly that mounts the adapters its descendants relay upward.
root module collection-review tagged [dispatch]

// The neutral protocol vocabulary a feature needs to build an adapter, with the
// schema and result shapes a tool contribution's signature names. It reaches
// every descendant, but only dispatch-classified source can import it: the core
// owners and the pure view carry no `dispatch`.
expose-src InvocationContext, ProtocolFacilities, McpToolContribution, ToolInvocation, ToolInputSchema, ToolResult from "interfaces/protocol.ts" to descendants

// The configured system itself, for any owner's tests, with the shapes its
// signature names. They are new testing-owned bindings, so they carry this
// owner's test profile and no production source anywhere can import them.
expose-test createTestSystem, TestSystem, McpSession from "setup.ts" to descendants

// The application router's type, for the shell that builds a client from it
// and the connected view that names that client. It is a same-owner alias of
// the assembly's own type, and the router's type is the declared return type
// of `assembleRouter`, which therefore travels with it; the rest of `assembly.ts`
// stays private. `ProtocolRouter` is the router type that return type, and
// each feature factory's, is written as. All three carry this owner's
// `dispatch` tag and no browser promise: the core owners and the pure view see
// them and can import them in neither form, and the owners that can import
// them do so as types.
expose-src AppRouter, assembleRouter, ProtocolRouter from "interfaces/protocol.ts" to descendants

// The contract `assembleRouter`'s declared return type states: each feature's
// procedure record and the vocabulary those records are written in. It travels
// wherever the router type does. The shell's descendants already receive the
// vocabulary from the shell; the root exposes it again so that every owner
// seeing the router type, the testing module included, also sees the types
// that describe it.
expose-sub CatalogProcedures, ReviewsProcedures, RecordId, recordIdSchema, revisionScopeSchema, ReviewStatus, reviewStatusSchema, Finding, findingSchema, Observation, observationSchema from workspace to descendants
